-- title:
--   Full Slice Product Left To Zero Le One
-- statement:
--   **The full-slice product-left family is within unit squared distance of zero.**
--
--   Let $(q,m,d)$ have a field model, let $S$ be a symmetric strategy on the successor space, let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family, and assume that the state of $S$ is normalized. Pull each evaluated-slice question back to its corresponding full-slice question. The raw operator family `fullSliceProductLeft` on those pulled-back questions has state-dependent squared distance at most one from the zero operator family under the uniform evaluated-slice distribution:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_S\!\left(\mathcal U,
--   q\mapsto\mathrm{fullSliceProductLeft}\bigl(\mathrm{fullSliceQuestionOfEvaluatedSlice}(q)\bigr),
--   \mathbf{0},1\right).
--   $$
--
--   The unit bound follows from normalization and the positive operator bounds in the product construction. It is used to control the zero endpoint in `fullSliceCommutation_of_evaluated_on_evaluated_questions`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.fullSliceProductLeft_to_zero_le_one`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/Transport/FullSlice/ZeroBounds.lean#L212-L234

